# Text encoding (never break characters)

When creating or editing HTML, Markdown, JS string literals in docs, or any text file in this repo:

1. **Save as UTF-8** (no Latin-1 / Windows-1252 / mixed encodings).
2. Prefer **ASCII punctuation** in HTML/docs served in iframes or downloaded by staff:
   - Use `-` instead of em/en dashes
   - Use `'` and `"` instead of curly/smart quotes
   - Use `...` instead of ellipsis character
   - Use `/` or `|` instead of middle-dot `·` if unsure
3. Always include `<meta charset="utf-8" />` at the top of HTML documents.
4. After writing HTML/docs, **verify** the file decodes as UTF-8 (no `UnicodeDecodeError`, no replacement `` in the browser).
5. Never copy-paste from Word/PDF into a file without checking encoding.

If the user sees black-diamond `` or ``, treat it as a **P0 encoding bug** and rewrite the file cleanly.
